            "summary": "Lithuania's State Defense Council (chaired by President Naus\u0117da) authorized the Ministry of National Defence to contract with Finnish producer Patria for 936 Patria 6x6 wheeled APCs. Contract expected in 2027; approximately 300 vehicles to arrive by 2030. The vehicles will replace Lithuania's aging M113 fleet and support multiple roles (air defense, medical, logistics, reconnaissance, CBRN). Lithuania joins the CAVS program (Finland, Latvia, Sweden, Denmark, Norway, Germany, UK, Ukraine). President Naus\u0117da conditioned the deal on Lithuanian industrial participation \u2014 a portion of funds must remain in the Lithuanian economy. Announced the same day: the Lithuanian Armed Forces established the ANBO unit to develop long-range drone capabilities, described as the formalization of approximately two years of drone training development since 2024.",
