            "summary": "Darius Kuliesius, deputy head of Lithuania's communications regulator, told Reuters that Russia increased GPS spoofing antennas in Kaliningrad from 3 in early 2025 to 36 now, broadcasting false signals at a radius of up to 450 km. The interference \u2014 described as 'systemic, permanent, unending Russian provocation against European security' \u2014 began sporadically around the 2023 NATO Vilnius Summit and has become continuous. The coverage area encompasses Estonia, Latvia, Lithuania, most of Poland, parts of Finland, Sweden, and Belarus. Civilian infrastructure effects are already being observed (Klaip\u0117da bus GPS tracking systems fail during spikes). Latvia separately announced deployment of mobile drone intercept teams to its Russian and Belarusian borders in the same week.",
